description:
## Goal

Separate "API object representation" (serde_json::Value) from "wire format" (JSON bytes vs protobuf bytes) behind a trait. This makes handler unit tests format-agnostic, isolates the proto re-encoding path, and makes it easy to add new serializers (e.g. full typed proto) without touching handlers.

## Design

```rust
// crates/apiserver/src/serializer.rs (new file)
pub(crate) trait ApiSerializer: Send + Sync {
    fn serialize(&self, val: &serde_json::Value) -> bytes::Bytes;
    fn content_type(&self) -> &'static str;
}

pub(crate) struct JsonSerializer;
impl ApiSerializer for JsonSerializer {
    fn serialize(&self, val: &serde_json::Value) -> bytes::Bytes {
        bytes::Bytes::from(val.to_string())
    }
    fn content_type(&self) -> &'static str { "application/json" }
}

pub(crate) struct ProtoSerializer;
impl ApiSerializer for ProtoSerializer {
    fn serialize(&self, val: &serde_json::Value) -> bytes::Bytes {
        crate::proto::encode_proto_response(val)
    }
    fn content_type(&self) -> &'static str {
        "application/vnd.kubernetes.protobuf"
    }
}
```

The content_type Tower middleware (`content_type.rs`) selects the serializer based on the Accept header and injects it (or a flag) into the response pipeline. Handlers themselves never inspect Accept — they always produce `serde_json::Value`, and the serializer layer handles wire format.

## Benefits

- Handler tests use `JsonSerializer` — no proto logic to worry about
- Proto path is fully isolated — easy to swap in typed proto per-kind later
- Adding a new format (e.g. CBOR, YAML) is one new impl, zero handler changes
- Cleaner than the current Tower middleware that intercepts and re-encodes after the fact

## Scope

- New file `crates/apiserver/src/serializer.rs` (~50 lines)
- Refactor `content_type.rs` to use the trait (~30 lines changed)
- No handler changes required if the middleware layer stays as-is
- Tests: JsonSerializer and ProtoSerializer round-trip tests

## Note

This is a prerequisite for mayor-fullproto (full typed proto support) but has standalone value for testability regardless.

## Not blocked by anything.
